      "writtenOn": "2026-04-07T03:21:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "SGTM, but I think some way to specifically swap two change IDs is really important. Like if I do a split then try uploading and realise I\u0027ve associated the wrong one, it\u0027d be nice to be able to just swap them instead of a several-step process where it\u0027s easy to make mistakes.\n\nThat was why I thought it\u0027d be good to have a specific subcommand for dealing with various operations on the change-id. WDYT? I feel like we\u0027d struggle to put that in metaedit with a convenient API.\n\nFYI I\u0027ve made a patch to git that fixes the compatibility on the git end.\n\nhttps://lore.kernel.org/git/CAH7WC73-4p0RrqKNSh2G-xfpfO7QHZiXHbU_UFRkM3Q\u003dbMWTDw@mail.gmail.com/T/#u",
